Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Benjamin Peterson (BitBucket: [gutworth](http://bitbucket.org/gutworth), GitHub: [gutworth](http://github.com/gutworth))**:\n\n---\n\nAnother reason for this heuristic occurred to me: Many commonly used global names like classes and modules are more nicely displayed by their name rather than their repr.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112200542/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pytestbot","id":12873537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODczNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12873537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytestbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112200545","html_url":"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/171#issuecomment-112200545","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/171","id":112200545,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDExMjIwMDU0NQ==","user":{"login":"pytestbot","id":12873537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODczNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12873537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytestbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-01-10T00:56:07Z","updated_at":"2015-06-15T20:34:09Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Floris Bruynooghe (BitBucket: [flub](http://bitbucket.org/flub), GitHub: [flub](http://github.com/flub))**:\n\n---\n\nThe attached patch has one test failure:\n\n```\n__________________________________ TestAssertionRewrite.test_attribute ___________________________________\n\nself = <test_assertrewrite.TestAssertionRewrite instance at 0x1210440>\n\n    def test_attribute(self):\n        class X(object):\n            g = 3\n        ns = {\"X\" : X, \"x\" : X()}\n        def f():\n            assert not x.g\n>       assert getmsg(f, ns) == \"\"\"assert not 3\n     +  where 3 = x.g\"\"\"\nE       assert 'assert not 3... 0x12d4d90>.g' == 'assert not 3\\...where 3 = x.g'\nE           assert not 3\nE         -  +  where 3 = <test_assertrewrite.X object at 0x12d4d90>.g\nE         +  +  where 3 = x.g\n\ntesting/test_assertrewrite.py:245: AssertionError\n```\n\nWhich is exactly the last issue you mention, I think it might be possible to add another test to the display logic which checks if the name is a class _and_ is a global.  Do you reckon this is